00:45:44.363 --> 00:45:45.810
if you had more chapters,

00:45:45.810 --> 00:45:48.010
who would you have added
back into the book?

00:45:49.290 --> 00:45:51.960
- You know, actually-
- You're good?

00:45:51.960 --> 00:45:52.833
- Yeah, I'm good.

00:45:54.103 --> 00:45:55.650
Like, I enjoyed spending time with them,

00:45:55.650 --> 00:45:56.751
but at a certain point,

00:45:56.751 --> 00:45:58.380
I'm like I didn't wanna spend
any more time with them.

00:45:58.380 --> 00:46:00.730
Like I'm writing this
book about the Astors now

00:46:02.370 --> 00:46:04.590
and there's a lot of dreadful Astors.

00:46:04.590 --> 00:46:05.880
I mean, they're just sort of dreadful

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:06.713
and after a while,

00:46:06.713 --> 00:46:08.550
you just don't wanna spend
any more time with them.

00:46:08.550 --> 00:46:11.310
They make the Vanderbilts
seem, I don't know,

00:46:11.310 --> 00:46:13.626
more fun. (laughing)
(Mary, audience laughing)

00:46:13.626 --> 00:46:15.150
Yeah.

00:46:15.150 --> 00:46:17.850
